<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>

<p><b>CUETConnect</b> is a peer-to-peer campus delivery coordination platform designed for students of the Chittagong University of Engineering &amp; Technology (CUET). The platform enables students who need items from the city to post delivery requests, while fellow students who are already traveling can accept and fulfill those requests for a reward.</p>

<p>The project was proposed as an Internet Programming course project with the objective of building a modern, real-time web application that solves a genuine campus problem. The key features implemented include:</p>

<ul>
<li><b>Google OAuth authentication</b> with automatic profile creation via Supabase Auth.</li>
<li><b>Complete delivery lifecycle management</b> — create, accept, track progress, complete, rate, and cancel requests.</li>
<li><b>Real-time WebSocket-powered chat</b> between requester and deliverer using Supabase Realtime.</li>
<li><b>Live notifications</b> with unread count badges and real-time updates.</li>
<li><b>Gamification system</b> — star ratings, achievement badges (Reliable, Elite Traveler, Legendary, 5-Star), earnings tracking, and a competitive leaderboard.</li>
<li><b>Responsive dark/light theme</b> with mobile-first design.</li>
<li><b>Bookmark system</b> for saving interesting delivery requests.</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Technologies used:</b> React 19, Vite 7.3, Tailwind CSS v4, React Router v7, Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Realtime, RLS), Lucide React, and Vercel for deployment.</p>

<p><b>Live Demo:</b> <a href="https://delivery-request-dashboard-ui.vercel.app/">https://delivery-request-dashboard-ui.vercel.app/</a></p>
<p><b>GitHub:</b> <a href="https://github.com/starboy1402/BringIT_Delivery_System">https://github.com/starboy1402/BringIT_Delivery_System</a></p>

<div class="pagebreak"></div>

<h2>2. Project Recap and Requirements Analysis</h2>

<h3>2.1 Original Objectives (from Proposal)</h3>
<p>The original proposal outlined the following objectives:</p>
<ul>
<li>Build a responsive web application for peer-to-peer delivery coordination among CUET students.</li>
<li>Implement secure user authentication restricted to CUET students.</li>
<li>Enable delivery request creation with item details, pickup/dropoff locations, reward, and urgency levels.</li>
<li>Provide a real-time feed to browse, search, and filter delivery requests.</li>
<li>Implement a delivery lifecycle: post → accept → in-progress → complete → rate.</li>
<li>Add real-time communication between requester and deliverer.</li>
<li>Build a gamification system with leaderboard, ratings, and badges.</li>
<li>Support dark/light themes and responsive mobile design.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2 Motivation</h3>
<p>CUET is located in Raozan, Chittagong — approximately 25 km from the city center. Students frequently need items (books, electronics, food, lab supplies) from the city but traveling costs 2-3 hours round trip. Meanwhile, many students commute daily and could carry items for peers. There was no organized platform to coordinate this — students relied on informal social media posts which were unreliable and lacked accountability. CUETConnect was proposed to solve this problem.</p>

