<h2>3. System Architecture and Design</h2>

<h3>3.1 Architecture Overview</h3>
<p>CUETConnect uses a <b>client-heavy SPA architecture</b> with Supabase as the Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS). Unlike traditional MERN or Django stacks, there is no custom backend server. All server-side logic — authentication, database queries, real-time subscriptions, and access control — is handled by Supabase's managed PostgreSQL instance with Row Level Security (RLS) policies.</p>

<p><b>UML Component Diagram:</b></p>
<p><i>[Insert UML Diagram Here — showing React SPA → Supabase Auth / Supabase DB / Supabase Realtime]</i></p>

<p><b>Data Flow:</b></p>
<pre>
User Browser (React SPA)
    │
    ├── Auth Flow: Google OAuth → Supabase Auth → JWT Token → localStorage
    │
    ├── Data Queries: Supabase JS SDK → PostgREST API → PostgreSQL (RLS enforced)
    │
    ├── Real-time: Supabase Realtime → WebSocket → postgres_changes events
    │
    └── RPC Functions: supabase.rpc() → plpgsql functions (SECURITY DEFINER)
</pre>

